--- a/salt/cache/CODEMANIFEST
+++ b/salt/cache/CODEMANIFEST
@@ -73,6 +73,25 @@ Annotations: |
       Delete the on-disk entry for `key` in `bank` (or the whole `bank` directory if `key` is
       omitted).
 
+"Cache::Sqlite3Backend()":
+  location: sqlite3_cache.py
+  annotations: |
+    An alternate backend driver, selected via the cache option, that stores every bank/key
+    entry as a row in a single on-disk SQLite database file opened with the standard-library
+    sqlite3 module -- no extra service or third-party package required. Unlike
+    `LocalFSBackend`'s per-entry files, all entries share one file and one bank/ckey-keyed
+    table, so data written before a master restart is read back afterwards from that same
+    file. Connections are cached per database path and process id so a forked master worker
+    never reuses a connection opened by its parent.
+  methods:
+    "store(bank: str, key: str, data: object, cachedir: str)": |
+      Serialize `data` and upsert the row for `bank`/`key` in the SQLite database under
+      cachedir.
+    "fetch(bank: str, key: str, cachedir: str) -> data:object": |
+      Read and deserialize the row for `bank`/`key`, or an empty value if it doesn't exist.
+    "flush(bank: str, key: str | None, cachedir: str | None)": |
+      Delete the row for `key` in `bank` (or every row for `bank` if `key` is omitted).
+
 ---
 
 Author: Goga
